  "description": "KAXDUK crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C50 H98 Dy4 Mn4 N10 O34 4+,1.6(Cl1 1-),0.4(N3 1-),2(N1 O3 1-),1.6(C1 H4 O1),2.4(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1A (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2A (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 13 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.213-3.654 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.84-113.40°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Mn4Dy4(OH)6(H2L)2(H3L)2(PhCO2)2(N3)2(MeOH)4]Cl1.6(N3)0.4(NO3)2·2.4H2O·1.6MeOH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
